Yes!  In programming, we often want to perform the same action over and over again, like counting from 1 to 10.  To do this, we can use a loop.  Here’s an example in C:

for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    cout << i << " ";
}

This loop will print the numbers 1 to 10, one by one.  There are many different types of loops, and I could explain them all in detail, but I’ll just give you an example of one more common type: a while loop.  In this case, we want to repeat some action as long as a condition is true.  Here’s an example in C:

int i = 1;
while (i <= 10) {
    cout << i << " ";
    i++;
}

This loop will print the numbers 1 to 10, one by one.  It’s the same as the for loop above, except that we use a while loop instead of a for loop.

